WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.780
Picture a resident asking

2
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:03.200
a simple question.

3
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:03.520
We gave

4
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.900
this project support,

5
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.620
so what was

6
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.960
promised in return?

7
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.580
That should be

8
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.040
easy to answer.

9
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.180
Public support should come

10
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:11.030
with a receipt.

11
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.700
That's where Promise

12
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.940
Ledger comes in.

13
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:14.420
It's a tool

14
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.260
for city housing staff.

15
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.280
It gathers the scattered

16
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.400
paperwork builds one checkable

17
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.040
record for each deal.

18
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:21.760
It shows what

19
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:22.720
was promised,

20
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:23.980
what was approved,

21
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.080
what was signed,

22
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:25.980
what's still owed.

23
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.480
Every line links back

24
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.580
to the exact page

25
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:29.400
it came from so

26
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.910
anyone can check it.

27
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.040
It doesn't make

28
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.200
legal findings.

29
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.300
It simply helps people

30
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.440
see clearly so

31
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:36.100
they can decide

32
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.250
what happens next.

